{
  "requirement": "In a design session with no code to write, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to stop after the requirements commit.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement has one clause: \"In a design session with no code to write, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to stop after the requirements commit.\" It sets no library, algorithm, signature, type, field or delegation interface. It constrains only what the skill document tells agents, which is observable behavior of the skill text. So it has no structural obligation that needs implementation evidence.\n\nThe root, `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, does contain the direction. In `section[Habeas%20requirements]/section[Workflow]`, step 5, \"Commit\", ends with: \"In a design session with no code to write, stop here.\" Step 5 is the requirements commit: it commits the agreed book text before any code. So the skill directs agents to stop after that commit.\n\nThe wording or placement of that sentence is a discretionary authoring choice. I found no missing root or gap.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one behavioral obligation. In a design session with no code to write, the `habeas-requirements` skill must tell agents to stop after the requirements commit.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_stops_after_the_commit_in_a_design_session]` covers it. The test finds the workflow step of the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill that contains \"all groups together\", which is the commit step. It then calls `assert_text_in_order` on that step's text. The helper panics unless \"then commit it\" appears first and \"In a design session with no code to write, stop here\" appears after it.\n\nThese assertions enforce both parts of the clause: the design-session condition and the instruction to stop at the commit. If the sentence were missing, reworded, or moved before the commit instruction, the test would fail.\n\n`workflow_steps` joins each step's indented continuation lines and collapses their whitespace. The phrase in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is wrapped across two lines, and this collapsing is why the single-line phrase in the test matches it.\n\nThe helpers `step`, `step_of`, `workflow_steps` and `assert_text_in_order` are reached from the marked test, so they need no markers of their own. The requirement has no other modes or boundaries, so I found no gap.",
